WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.330
Hey guys, this is Vadim with Max Tech and
today I’m gonna tell you why the 2018 iPad

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.759
is the best bang for the buck iPad yet!

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:13.680
But wait, don’t go and buy it just yet,
I’ll explain why in just a minute.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.280
First of all, it’s the first and only non-Pro
iPad to support the Apple Pencil.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.750
Previously, you’d have to spend at least
$650 to get the cheapest iPad Pro, just to

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.750
use the Apple Pencil.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.430
And even though the experience isn’t as
nice as on the iPad Pro, with its laminated

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.550
display and ProMotion technology, you’re
still getting a lot for your money.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.460
For example, you’re still getting the same
great design and build quality, decent speakers

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.070
and all the other bells and whistles.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:43.510
It’ll do basically everything you want and
expect an iPad to do, for a heck of a lot

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.140
less than other iPads, even less than the
iPad Mini 4.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.749
Most people want an iPad to do things like
surf the web, do work for school, use the

00:00:51.749 --> 00:00:56.550
apple pencil, use apps, watch movies, play
games, and basic stuff like that.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.860
The 2018 iPad, does all of those things, and
it does them well.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:04.220
Obviously nowhere near as well as any of the
iPad Pros, but you’re saving half or more

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:05.220
of your cash.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.220
The reality of it is that the iPad Pro is
overkill for most people.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.610
It offers tons of features and incredible
amounts of power, but most people would actually

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:18.470
be better off saving some cash and going for
the regular iPad, and trust me, they’ll

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.050
be extremely happy with it.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.340
Let’s start with the display.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:26.960
It’s 9.7” size is great for most uses,
like reading an eBook, taking notes with the

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.570
Apple Pencil, watching YouTube videos or shows
on Netflix and playing games.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:36.630
It’s got better than 1080P resolution and
it’s using IPS technology, so it offers

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.170
great viewing angles.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.750
The size of the iPad itself is great for portability.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:41.870
You can easily fit it

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:46.130
The speakers also sound pretty decent and
they’re loud enough for most use cases.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.950
The only downside is that there are only speakers
on the bottom side of the iPad, so if you’re

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:55.010
watching something in landscape mode, it feels
a bit weird for all the sound to come from

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:58.400
one end instead of true stereo like on the
iPad Pros.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.550
On the plus side, it’s still packing a headphone
jack, unlike the 2018 iPad Pro, so it’s

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.870
easy to plug in a pair of stereo headphones.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:10.609
In terms of performance, everything is pretty
snappy, but definitely not as quick and smooth

00:02:10.609 --> 00:02:16.969
as the iPad Pro, especially the newer models
which come with ProMotion 120hz display technology.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:22.249
Going from one of those models to the 9.7”
iPads 60hz display makes every animation seem

00:02:22.249 --> 00:02:26.660
a bit choppy, but you’ll never notice is
if you haven’t used a newer iPad Pro.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.030
Compared to some Android tablets, however,
the performance sticks around and doesn’t

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.829
start to slow down after a few months.

00:02:32.829 --> 00:02:38.430
Looking at raw performance, the iPad isn’t
that much slower than the 2017 iPad Pro, especially

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:39.989
in single core tasks.

00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:44.719
In multi-core, there’s a noticeable jump
with the Pro, but the 9.7” iPads performance

00:02:44.719 --> 00:02:47.230
is still impressive for its low price.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.549
Graphics performance is where you’ll see
the biggest difference, with more than double

00:02:50.549 --> 00:02:56.870
the score on the 2017 10.5” Pro, and more
than triple the score with the 2018 Pro.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:01.109
With that big of a difference, many people
have asked if the 9.7” iPad can play games

00:03:01.109 --> 00:03:03.269
like Fortnite, so we tested it out.

00:03:03.269 --> 00:03:08.099
We noticed it limits graphics quality to Medium
and 30 frames per second, unlike the newer

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:11.989
iPad Pros that can run at high settings at
60 frames per second.

00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:15.769
The nice thing is that you can connect a controller
like the Steelseries Nimbus.

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:20.279
In game, there were some dropped frames and
it wasn’t perfectly smooth but it was definitely

00:03:20.279 --> 00:03:21.279
playable.

00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:25.090
You could actually have an enjoyable experience
playing Fortnite, so it should work pretty

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.749
well for almost any other game out there.

00:03:26.749 --> 00:03:28.340
Now let’s talk about the cameras.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:33.180
Honestly, the front-facing camera is horrible,
so forget about taking selfies with it.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.959
The rear camera isn’t too bad but it’s
way behind any of the newer iPhones.

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:41.270
Finally, Apple pencil support is what makes
this an iPad this cheap, really great.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:46.829
Not only that, but the 9.7” iPad also supports
the Logitech Crayon, which the iPad Pro doesn’t

00:03:46.829 --> 00:03:47.829
support, and it’s also twice as cheap as
the regular Apple Pencil.

00:03:47.829 --> 00:03:51.480
The drawing and note-taking experience is
much better on the newer iPad Pros since they

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.690
have ProMotion technology which reduces lag,
along with the laminated display, but for

00:03:56.690 --> 00:04:00.739
the low price of $329, it still works great
on the iPad.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:05.559
In terms of battery life, the iPad is pretty
great, similar to the 10.5” iPad Pro, which

00:04:05.559 --> 00:04:09.629
lasts around 8 hours straight while watching
a video with brightness set to a pretty high

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:10.629
80%.

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:15.410
You’ll definitely get more than this since
you won’t have the screen on all the time.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:19.320
Overall, the 9.7” iPad is the perfect iPad
for almost everyone.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.580
It just does what you need it to do for a
relatively cheap price.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.580
In fact, it’s currently on sale for only
$250 on Amazon.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.140
We’ll have a link to that sale in the video
description.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:33.080
Yes, the Pro is much better in many ways,
but it’s actually overkill for a lot of

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.990
people, especially the 2018 model.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.270
Now wait, don’t buy the 9.7” iPad just
yet.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:44.570
There have been many rumors of two iPads coming
out soon, the iPad Mini 5 and the 2019 iPad,

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:48.450
and we’re expecting them to be released
at the end of next month, so if you can wait,

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.220
I would highly recommend that you do so.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.430
We’re not sure what changes will be made
to the new model, but it’s definitely gonna

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.430
be improved.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:57.580
This has been Vadim with Max Tech, thanks
for watching and make sure to subscribe so

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.490
you don’t miss out on more videos like this
one.

